        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 46.0
      },
      "display_window_mm": {
        "width": 52.0,
        "height": 25.0
      },
      "intake": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 80.0
      },
      "usb": {
        "face": "bottom",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 62.0
      },
      "cmf": {
        "material": "rABS",
        "finish": "textured_light",
        "color": "warm greige NCS S 2005-Y20R",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "pad_print",
          "laser_etch"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the pebble plan outline: continuous tangent arc with no flat side wall, minimum plan radius 13.5 mm, so the front view reads as one soft solid rather than a box with fillets.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Display must stay >= 50 mm wide with a 25 mm active height and sit at 46% of front-face height, giving ~2.7 m legibility at the sofa; do not shrink the window or push it lower to win cost.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "No visible fasteners: the parting line is a 0.15 mm shadow gap on the side wall only, and all screws are reached through the bottom USB recess. Any visible screw boss or clip window breaks the brief.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Front face carries a 2 mm forward crown; the display recess is 0.6 mm deep with a 0.6 mm shadow gap around the window, so the screen sits in a soft dimple, not a raised bezel.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Use rABS with a light mould texture (VDI 27-30 equivalent) as the base finish; pad-print the front wordmark in the same hue and laser-etch the bottom label. Soft-touch paint is a costed option only, not a baseline.",
          "category": "sustainability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Keep nominal wall at 1.8 mm, ribs at 1.2 mm, and the display recess wall at 1.6 mm so the 29 mm pebble stays inside the 18 CNY BOM while surviving a 0.6 m living-room drop.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The reference desk unit is a rounded rectangle; this variant rounds the plan until the sides become tangent arcs, which is the cheapest way to get a furniture-like pebble from a two-plate injection tool. 118 x 68 x 29 mm sits inside the 125 x 75 x 30 mm contract with 7 mm of length margin for the tool's shut-off and 1 mm of height margin for the crown; at 1.8 mm nominal wall the housing weighs about 74 g, leaving ~14 g for the display module, sensor, PCB and battery under the 180 g cap. The 52 x 25 mm display window is larger than the reference's 44 x 20 mm because the sofa viewing assumption (2.5-3 m) needs either size or contrast; size is cheaper than a brighter panel, and the front-crown recess keeps a 0.6 mm shadow gap that reads as a black border without a separate bezel part. Intake is a 38 mm wide arc of seven 1.2 x 4 mm slots centred at 80% of the front face, below the display and above the bottom curve, so the sensor sees room air and the slots disappear into the pebble's shading. USB-C sits on the bottom face at 62% depth, angled 12 degrees so a cable can enter while the unit stands; the recess doubles as the service access for the two M2.5 screws, which is the only way to hide fasteners without adding a cosmetic cap. rABS with a light mould texture meets the sustainability priority and the Q2 default (texture instead of soft-touch paint), while pad-print and laser-etch are low-cost secondary ops that keep the BOM inside the 18 CNY ceiling. The main risk is the 13.5 mm plan radius thinning the side wall where the two plates shut off; the answer is to move the parting line to the widest point of the pebble and keep the side wall at 2.0 mm locally, which IA6 protects."
    },
